course: dictionary
lesson: 8688
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word «seine» can name a fishing net, be a verb for catching fish, or name a river. Read the words around it to decide.
explain: The capital letter is a clue too. «Paris, the capital of France, stands on the river Seine.» The capital S and the word river tell you this is a place name, not a net. Ask yourself: which meaning fits here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Verbs work the same way. «The crew seined the bay before the tide came in» means they caught fish with a seine net, because seined is an action word, and the crew is doing something with the net. When you see seine in a sentence about fishing, look for a net or a catch. When you see it with a capital S near a city, think of a river.
fact: A seine is a large fishing net that hangs straight down in the water, with floats on top and weights at the bottom.
fact: To seine means to catch fish with this kind of net.
fact: The Seine, with a capital S, is the river that flows through Paris in France.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is right: a capital S and the word river point to the place name.
fact: The French word «Seine» sounds like «sen».
exercise: «The fishers hauled the seine to the shore, full of fish.» What is a seine here? | A long bridge over a river | A kind of hat worn by fishers | A small boat with a sail | *A large fishing net with floats on top and weights at the bottom
exercise: «Paris stands on the river Seine.» In this sentence, what is the Seine? | A large fishing net | *A river that flows through Paris | To catch fish with a net | A French word for fish
exercise: «The crew seined the bay before the tide came in.» What does seined mean? | Swam to the shore | Painted the boat blue | *Caught fish with a seine net | Sailed quickly across the bay
test: In «They used a seine to catch cod», what kind of word is seine? | Capital letter | Verb | Adjective | *Noun
test: Which sentence uses the Seine as a place? | They hauled the seine to shore. | *Boats sail along the Seine past the bridges of Paris. | The crew seined the bay at dawn. | Scientists count fish with seine nets.
exam: What does «seine» mean in «Scientists use seine nets to count fish in rivers and the sea»? | *A large fishing net | A kind of fish | A river in France | To swim quickly
